# keep existing links working

# The feed is generated from the articles table on the bot now, not in this
# repo. 301 so readers that cached the old URL pick up the move. Static rules,
# so they go above the wildcards.
/news/feed.xml https://api.umkl.co.uk/feed.xml 301
/news/feed https://api.umkl.co.uk/feed.xml 301

# Article pages are rendered by news/article.html from the news API, keyed off
# the slug in the path.
#
# The destination is the clean URL, without .html. Cloudflare Pages normalises
# `article.html` to `article` and answers a request for the .html form with a
# 308, so naming it explicitly turns the rewrite into a redirect - the browser
# ends up on /news/article with no slug in the path, and articlerender.js has
# nothing to load.
#
# Two path segments are needed so these leave /news/, /news/article and
# /news/index.html alone.
/news/:date/:slug/ /news/article 200
/news/:date/:slug /news/article 200